<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lee Hsien Loong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1952</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lee Hsien Loong is a Singaporean politician, the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lee-kuan-yew">Lee Kuan Yew</a>, who served as the country's third prime minister from 2004 to 2024 as leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-action-party">People's Action Party</a>. His government oversaw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>'s growth as a centre of finance and technology and its response to the 2008 financial crisis and the COVID-19 pandemic. He was succeeded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lawrence-wong">Lawrence Wong</a> in 2024.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lee-hsien-loong.jpg" alt="Lee Hsien Loong" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_lee_hsien_loong_2026.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
